    "html": "<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"/help-assets/inventory.png\" alt=\"Itemized inventory dashboard showing In Stock products, sidebar counts, and location tree\"></p>\n<p>Get from a fresh itemized instance to tracking your pantry, fridge, and freezer in a few minutes.</p>\n<h2 id=\"create-your-administrator-account\">Create your administrator account</h2>\n<p>When you open itemized for the first time, the setup screen prompts you to create the initial <strong>Admin</strong> account with an email address and password (at least 8 characters). You can add other household members or configure OIDC later in <a href=\"/help/configure/accounts-and-sso\">Accounts and SSO</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"set-up-locations-and-categories\">Set up locations and categories</h2>\n<p>On a fresh instance, the home page displays a <strong>Get Started</strong> card with a 1-click <strong>Load Starter Setup</strong> button that adds a ready-to-use grocery-store category list and common household locations (with freezers pre-flagged). You can also customize or build your own tree anytime in <strong>Locations</strong> and <strong>Categories</strong>, or type a new name directly inside the Category or Location dropdowns while adding or scanning a product to create it on the spot.</p>\n<h2 id=\"add-your-first-product\">Add your first product</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Press <code>n</code> (or select <strong>+ New Product</strong>) to open the New Product form.</li>\n<li>Enter a clear name following the <code>Item, Variety, Detail</code> style (such as <em>Milk, Whole, Organic</em>). Itemized checks for similar existing products as you type to prevent duplicates.</li>\n<li>Choose a <strong>Category</strong>, <strong>Default Location</strong>, and optional <strong>Minimum Stock</strong> level.</li>\n<li>Leave <strong>Calculate due date from rolling average of recent purchases</strong> checked, or uncheck it to set a fixed number of days.</li>\n<li>Select <strong>Save Product</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"record-stock-with-scan-action\">Record stock with Scan / Action</h2>\n<p>Select <strong>Scan / Action</strong> from the sidebar (or the bottom dock on mobile), stay in <strong>Purchase</strong> mode, and scan a retail barcode or pick your product. Enter the quantity, confirm the location and due date, and submit.</p>\n<h2 id=\"review-your-dashboard\">Review your dashboard</h2>\n<p>Use the sidebar filters to see what is <strong>In Stock</strong>, what is <strong>Due Soon</strong> or <strong>Overdue</strong>, and what needs restocking on your <strong>Shopping List</strong>.</p>\n",
    "searchText": "Getting started Complete first-run setup, add your first product, record stock, and check Due Soon and Shopping List. Get from a fresh itemized instance to tracking your pantry, fridge, and freezer in a few minutes. Create your administrator account When you open itemized for the first time, the setup screen prompts you to create the initial Admin account with an email address and password (at least 8 characters). You can add other household members or configure OIDC later in Accounts and SSO. Set up locations and categories On a fresh instance, the home page displays a Get Started card with a 1-click Load Starter Setup button that adds a ready-to-use grocery-store category list and common household locations (with freezers pre-flagged). You can also customize or build your own tree anytime in Locations and Categories, or type a new name directly inside the Category or Location dropdowns while adding or scanning a product to create it on the spot. Add your first product Press n (or select + New Product) to open the New Product form. Enter a clear name following the Item, Variety, Detail style (such as Milk, Whole, Organic). Itemized checks for similar existing products as you type to prevent duplicates. Choose a Category, Default Location, and optional Minimum Stock level. Leave Calculate due date from rolling average of recent purchases checked, or uncheck it to set a fixed number of days. Select Save Product. Record stock with Scan / Action Select Scan / Action from the sidebar (or the bottom dock on mobile), stay in Purchase mode, and scan a retail barcode or pick your product. Enter the quantity, confirm the location and due date, and submit. Review your dashboard Use the sidebar filters to see what is In Stock, what is Due Soon or Overdue, and what needs restocking on your Shopping List."
